  "live_records": {
    "q-138589": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138589",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 10 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample mean vector of $X.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the sample mean vector is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ are the individual observations (columns of $X$).\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{4}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
