    "q-138597": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138597",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample mean vector of $X.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the sample mean vector is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ are the individual observations (columns of $X$).\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{4}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-138597-a",
