    "q-137297": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137297",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
